A worked example to make simulation 51:

pymol session: manually dock L4 and L2 into PBP1B (pdb 5hlb). export 3 separate PDBs with PG following GLY and PA## nomenclature
51_pbp1b.pdb
51_donor_l4.pdb
51_acceptor_l2.pdb

charmm-gui: read and manipulate PBP1b pdb. apply terminal group patches and adjust protonation states. 
    produces step1_pdbreader.psf, crd, pdb (in a tgz)

    extract and rename to 51_pbp1b_cg.pdb, 51_pbp1b_cg.crd, 51_pbp1b_cg.psf

charmm: upload 51_acceptor_l2.pdb and 51_donor_l4.pdb to custom_files folder
    python setup_NPG.py 2 custom_files/51_donor_l4.pdb 
    charmm < build_NPG.inp > build_NPG_51_donor.out
    python setup_NPG.py 1 custom_files/51_acceptor_l2.pdb 
    charmm < build_NPG.inp > build_NPG_51_acceptor.out

each 51_donor_l4_export folder contains 51_donor_l4_l4 files (pdb, crd, psf) 
-l4 used to make l4 (no chain extension)
-51_donor_l4_32 would mean that l4 was used to make 51_donor_l4_32 (python setup_NPG.py 16 custom_files/51_donor_l4.pdb)

download results

make a new local folder, 51_assembly. combine files and manually rename

    51_pbp1b_cg.crd, 51_pbp1b_cg.psf -> 51_assembly_divisome.psf, crd
    51_donor_l4_l4.psf, crd -> 51_assembly_acceptor_l2.psf, crd
    51_donor_l4_l4.psf, crd -> 51_assembly_donor_l4.psf, crd

upload results

python setup_assembly.py 2 51_assembly 
    (breaks if "51_assembly/" is used)

charmm < assemble_docked_divisome.inp > 51_assembly_export/assemble_docked_divisome.out

download 51_assembly_export folder

spot check structures in pymol

run through charmm-gui multicomponent assembler
    CG-MCA will always split molecules apart unless merged into one psf/crd 
    CG-MCA will always identify unique segids and rename them according to its own internal logic
    CG-MCA assumes all patches, termini, etc are correct and does not have this step

=====Code analysis=======

The two steps make too many folders and require too much manual renaming of files. 
    51_donor_l4_export
    51_acceptor_l2_export
    51_assembly
    51_assembly_export

The second step is especially bad because it makes too many assumptions about the system
    There won't always be a donor and an acceptor (but if there are they must follow the GLYA/GLYD convention)
    The acceptor won't always be L2
    The protein component won't always represent the whole divisome (like PBP1B)

The external charmm-gui step cannot be skipped because the charmm scripts don't have patching functionality

Solution: Prepare one folder per unique sim and run one setup script AFTER doing charmm-gui patching 

    51_pbp1b_l4_l2
        51_pbp1b_cg.psf
        51_pbp1b_cg.crd
        51_donor_l4.pdb
        51_acceptor_l2.pdb

Assembly script runs 
    build NPG on L4
    build NPG on L2
    assemble psf/crd files together




